# pytest cache directory #

This directory contains data from the pytest's cache plugin,
which provides the `--lf` and `--ff` options, as well as the `cache` fixture.

**Do not** commit this to version control.

See [the docs](https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/cache.html) for more information.


# Ticket Management API

A REST API built using FastAPI, SQLModel, SQLite and Alembic to manage users, tickets and comments.

## Features
- User creation and retrieval
- Ticket CRUD operations
- Comment creation and retrieval
- Pagination and filtering by status and priority
- Input validation and error handling
- Database migrations using Alembic
- Integration tests using pytest and httpx
- Synthetic seed data

## Installation

Install dependencies:

```bash
uv sync
```

## Database Setup

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

## Run the API

```bash
uv run uvicorn ticket_api.main:app --reload
```

API: http://127.0.0.1:8000

Swagger documentation: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

## API Endpoints

### Users
- POST /users
- GET /users
- GET /users/{user_id}

### Tickets
- POST /tickets
- GET /tickets
- GET /tickets/{ticket_id}
- PATCH /tickets/{ticket_id}
- DELETE /tickets/{ticket_id}

### Comments
- POST /tickets/{ticket_id}/comments
- GET /tickets/{ticket_id}/comments

## Pagination and Filtering

Example:

```text
/tickets?skip=0&limit=10&status=open&priority=high
```

## Seed Data

```bash
uv run python -m ticket_api.seed
```

## Run Integration Tests

```bash
uv run pytest -v
```

Tests use a separate temporary SQLite database.

## Database Migrations

Create migration:

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "migration message"
```

Apply migration:

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

Check migration:

```bash
uv run alembic current
```

## Technology Stack
- Python
- FastAPI
- SQLModel
- SQLite
- Alembic
- Pytest
- HTTPX
- Uvicorn
